    "observed": "Explicit LOW_V1 remains slower than exact Leopard main in the three overlapping small K cells: about 54.6% slower for K=16,R=12,B=64, 5.4% slower for K=16,R=12,B=1024, and 74.5% slower for K=16,R=8,B=64 by public one-shot time. New-API AUTO selects LEGACY_HIGH_V1 rather than LOW_V1 when R<=K, so these explicit-low comparisons are not default-path regressions. LOW_V1 primarily covers R>K, which Leopard main rejects."
  },
  "conclusion": "The candidate passed independent algebra, safety, concurrency, backend, route-attribution, and isolated timing gates. Direct partial output removes the measured final scatter and gives credible target gains from 8.7% to 27.0% for reusable execution and 9.1% to 23.8% for public one-shot encode. No neighbor showed a credible regression greater than 2%.",
  "limitations": [
    "The authoritative campaign is single-core GF8 AVX2 on one Zen 5 host; other microarchitectures still rely on deterministic route bounds and correctness fallback.",
    "This optimization does not remove the broader explicit LOW_V1 small-shard overhead versus Leopard main for R<=K.",
    "Raw invocation evidence is retained under /tmp on this machine; this committed record contains its hashes and derived results but not the 12 MiB raw archive."
  ]
